  <footer class="provenance">
    <h2 class="prov-h">Sources, method and revisions</h2>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h6>Source of record</h6>
        <p>International Labour Organization, ILOSTAT, read through its SDMX data service (sdmx.ilo.org): the ILO modelled estimates ({edition}) and the ILO's processing of India's PLFS, NSS and Census unit data, plus administrative series. MoSPI's PLFS figures beside them come from the jobs guide's bundle. Data vintage <b id="prov-vintage">–</b>.</p>
        <p>Checked by hand against the ILO's labelled tables: unemployment rate 2024, 4.173%, flagged real; PLFS women's participation 2024, 34.389%.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Method</h6>
        <p>Values are as the ILO publishes them, with the ILO's own flags (real, unreliable, break in series) and uncertainty bounds kept on each series. Shares of employment by status, sector and class are computed from the ILO's counts. Nothing is estimated here.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Revisions and breaks</h6>
        <p>Each instrument (model, PLFS, NSS, Census, each administrative source) is its own series, never joined. Projection years sit in their own file. A new ILO edition replaces the modelled history, and the previous edition is archived.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>This guide</h6>
        <p>Version 1.0, built October 2026 from the ILO's November 2025 edition and its PLFS processing to {plfsYear}. Revised with each ILO edition.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
